m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Arginine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This network synthesizes arginine from simple C1, C2, and nitrogenous compounds available in prebiotic hydrothermal and surface environments. It integrates multiple plausible prebiotic pathways\u2014Strecker-like routes, reductive amination, condensation with cyanamide, and side-chain guanidinylation\u2014leveraging mineral catalysis, wet-dry cycling, and hydrothermal processes. Key intermediates include ornithine and guanidine, converging via diverse routes in variable ancient Earth settings.\n\nMOLECULES (14 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_003: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CH2O (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_005: C2H4O2 (acetic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_006: C3H7NO2 (alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_007: C5H12N2O2 (ornithine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: CH2N2 (cyanamide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: CH3NH2 (methylamine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: CH5N3 (guanidine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C4H9NO2 (diaminobutyric acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C6H14N4O2 (arginine) [target]\n  - mol_013: C3H7NO2 (beta-alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: N2 (nitrogen gas) [starting]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001, mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_005 (Acetic acid formation from CO2 reduction) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_004, mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_006 (Strecker-type synthesis of alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_003 -> mol_008 (Formation of cyanamide from HCN) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_006, mol_002, mol_008 -> mol_007 (Ornithine synthesis via reductive amination and extension) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_005: mol_008, mol_002 -> mol_010 (Guanidine formation from cyanamide and ammonia) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_005, mol_002, mol_004 -> mol_013 (Beta-alanine synthesis from acetic acid and ammonia) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_011, mol_004 -> mol_007 (Ornithine synthesis from diaminobutyric acid) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_013, mol_002, mol_004 -> mol_011 (Diaminobutyric acid synthesis from beta-alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_007, mol_010 -> mol_012 (Guanidinylation of ornithine to arginine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_010: mol_014, mol_002 -> mol_010 (Guanidine formation from ammonia and dinitrogen via reduction) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_001, mol_002 -> mol_009 (Methylamine from CO2 and H2 reduction) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_012: mol_009, mol_008, mol_002 -> mol_007 (Ornithine synthesis from methylamine and cyanamide) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Classic Strecker Route with Guanidinylation (5 steps)\n  - P2: Ornithine via Beta-Alanine and Diaminobutyric Acid Route (6 steps)\n  - P3: Ornithine Directly from Methylamine Pathway (5 steps)\n  - P4: Guanidine from N2 Reduction Route (4 steps)\n  - P5: Dual Route: Ornithine from Alanine and from Diaminobutyric Acid (7 steps)\n  - P6: Hydrothermal Reductive Pathway (7 steps)\n  - P7: Guanidine Formation from Surface Cyanamide in Multiple Uses (4 steps)\n  - P8: Beta-Alanine Centered Pathway (6 steps)\n  - P9: Methylamine-based Ornithine Synthesis with Surface-Centered Guanidine (5 steps)\n  - P10: Hydrothermal Guanidine with Surface Amino Acid Assembly (4 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK 