m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Arginine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: To construct plausible prebiotic synthesis networks for arginine, we leverage multiple, chemically justified routes rooted in minable geochemical, surface, and prebiotic pool environments. Core strategies include Strecker-type and reductive amination pathways for backbone construction, robust guanidinylation using cyanamide or urea derivatives, and key use of mineral- and UV-catalyzed conditions for activating and joining intermediates. Each reaction is atom- and charge-balanced to the extent permitted by prebiotic context, and all byproduct handling is explicit within the network.\n\nMOLECULES (15 nodes):\n  - mol_001: H2O (water) [starting]\n  - mol_002: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_003: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_005: CH2O (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_006: NH2CN (cyanamide) [starting]\n  - mol_007: CO(NH2)2 (urea) [starting]\n  - mol_008: C3H7NO2 (alanine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C4H9NO2 (ornithine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C6H14N4O2 (arginine) [target]\n  - mol_011: C2H5NO2 (glycine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C3H7N3O2 (guanidinopropionic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C3H7NO2 (beta-alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: NH2CONH2 (urea) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: C2H4N2 (ethylenediamine) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_002, mol_003, mol_005 -> mol_011, mol_001 (Aminonitrile formation (Strecker-type) from HCN and NH3) [Surface]\n  - rxn_002: mol_011, mol_005, mol_003 -> mol_013, mol_001 (Glycine chain extension by aldol/alkylation to beta-alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_013, mol_005, mol_003 -> mol_009, mol_001 (Amine homologation (Reductive amination) to ornithine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_004: mol_009, mol_006, mol_001 -> mol_010, mol_001 (Ornithine guanidinylation using cyanamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_011, mol_003, mol_001 -> mol_015, mol_004 (Reductive glycine pathway to ethylenediamine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_006: mol_015, mol_006, mol_005 -> mol_012, mol_001 (Ethylenediamine guanidinylation to produce guanidinopropionic acid) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_012, mol_005, mol_003 -> mol_009, mol_001 (Transamination/chain extension from guanidinopropionic acid to ornithine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_008: mol_006, mol_001 -> mol_014 (Urea synthesis from cyanamide and water) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_009, mol_014 -> mol_010, mol_001 (Ornithine guanidinylation using urea (alternative)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_010: mol_013, mol_005, mol_003 -> mol_009, mol_001 (Beta-alanine chain extension to ornithine (alternative)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_013, mol_006 -> mol_012, mol_001 (Direct guanidination of beta-alanine with cyanamide) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_012, mol_011 -> mol_009, mol_001 (Combination of guanidinopropionic acid and glycine to form ornithine (alternative condensation route)) [Biochemical]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Classic Strecker-to-Ornithine then guanidination by cyanamide (4 steps)\n  - P2: Strecker-to-beta-alanine to Ornithine then guanidination by urea (5 steps)\n  - P3: Direct guanidination of beta-alanine then chain extension (5 steps)\n  - P4: Ethylenediamine guanidination pathway (5 steps)\n  - P5: Reductive chain extension with alternative guanidination (5 steps)\n  - P6: Transamination route via surface and pool processes (5 steps)\n  - P7: Reductive amination via surface/hydrothermal alternation (4 steps)\n  - P8: Surface-only chain extension and guanidination (4 steps)\n  - P9: Double guanidination and condensation loop (5 steps)\n  - P10: Direct hydrothermal expansion and guanidination (4 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 12 reactions | 3 balanced as written | 0 balanceable with coefficients | 9 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: HCN + NH3 + CH2O -> C2H5NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: H-1, N+1, O-2 | balanceable if adding: CO2 as reactant; O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: C2H5NO2 + CH2O + NH3 -> C3H7NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: H+1, N+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO2 as product; CO as product; HCN as product\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: C3H7NO2 + CH2O + NH3 -> C4H9NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: C-1, H-2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO2 as product; CO as product; HCN as product\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: C2H5NO2 + NH3 + H2O -> C2H4N2 + CO2 | reactants minus products: C-1, H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: C2H4N2 + NH2CN + CH2O -> C3H7N3O2 + H2O | reactants minus products: C+1, H+3, N+1, O-2 | balanceable if adding: O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: C3H7N3O2 + CH2O + NH3 -> C4H9NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: C-1, H-2, N+2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO2 as product; CO as product; HCN as product\n  - rxn_010 UNBALANCED: C3H7NO2 + CH2O + NH3 -> C4H9NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: C-1, H-2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO2 as product; CO as product; HCN as product\n  - rxn_011 UNBALANCED: C3H7NO2 + NH2CN -> C3H7N3O2 + H2O | reactants minus products: C+1, O-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_012 UNBALANCED: C3H7N3O2 + C2H5NO2 -> C4H9NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: H-2, N+2, O+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\nFormula/structure inconsistencies:\n  - mol_009 (ornithine): stated formula C4H9NO2 disagrees with its InChI structure (stated minus InChI: C-1, H-3, N-1)\n  - mol_010: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_012: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_015 (ethylenediamine): stated formula C2H4N2 disagrees with its InChI structure (stated minus InChI: H-4)\nTreat this check as ground truth for mass and charge conservation. Reactions that cannot be balanced violate conservation: reflect this in chemical_feasibility and reaction_scores, list them in problematic_reactions, and name the specific reaction IDs (with the missing species, if hinted) in your feedback so the network can be corrected. Note that implausibly large inferred coefficients may also indicate a mis-specified reaction.\n=== END BALANCE CHECK ===\n\n\nPlease evaluate the network and respond with JSON:\n{\n    \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"<id>\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\"rxn_001\": 0.85, ...},\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"environmental_progression\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"target_achievement\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"feedback\": \"<pathway-specific feedback>\",\n            \"approved\": <true if confidence >= 0.8>,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_ids with issues\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\"improvements\"]\n        }\n    ],\n    \"best_pathway_id\": \"<id of best pathway>\",\n    \