ide.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Formamide seen as a central compound in prebiotic chemistry, easily formed by HCN hydrolysis (Saladino, 2012).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_012\",\n      \"name\": \"Amination of glycolaldehyde to serine (alternative chain extension)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"borate minerals\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"320-340K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"borate mineral\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"mild conditions\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Amination of glycolaldehyde by ammonia, with HCN providing cyano group; hydrolysis yields serine via Strecker-type route.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Extended Strecker sequences from C2 to C3 (serine) amines are supported by mineral-catalyzed surface chemistry (Saladino, 2012).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_013\",\n      \"name\": \"Formamide to glycine conversion\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_019\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_001\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_010\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"montmorillonite clay\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"320-340K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"montmorillonite clay\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"wet-dry cycling\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Condensation of formamide and ammonia with water elimination forms glycine.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Experimental mineral surface transformations produce glycine from formamide (Saladino, 2012; Di Mauro, 2021).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pathways\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"name\": \"Strecker-ornithine-guanidination sequence\",\n      \"description\": \"Classical sequential chain extension and guanidination: formaldehyde\u2192aminoacetonitrile\u2192glycine\u2192